pie''' is from chef Taylor Piercefield.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Pie ===\n* 1 container (8 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]] / 225 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[Cookbook:Sour Cream|sour cream]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (150 g) white [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]], [[Cookbook:Beat|beaten]]\n* 2½ cups (500 g) fresh [[Cookbook:Blueberry|blueberries]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. 9-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] (23 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]]) unbaked [[Cookbook:Pie Crust|pie shell]]\n\n=== Topping ===\n* 3 tablespoons flour\n* 3 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 3 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Pecan|pecans]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n=== Pie ===\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to [[Cookbook:Oven temperatures|400°F]] (200°C).\n# In a mixing bowl, combine sour cream, flour, sugar, vanilla, and egg.\n# [[Cookbook:Beat|Beat]] until very smooth.\n# Fold in blueberries.\n# Pour filling into pie shell.\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 25 minutes.\n\n=== Topping ===\n# In a small bowl, mix flour, butter and pecans, stirring well.\n# Sprinkle over pie and bake an additional 10 minutes.\n# Remove from oven.\n# Cool on [[Cookbook:Cooling Rack|wire rack]], then chill.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* A little [[Cookbook:Whipped Cream|whipped cream]] on top is a nice addition.\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:United States recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sour cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using blueberry]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]","isRecipe":false,"recipe":{"name":"Blueberry Cream Pie","nameAr"